Using the indexes

An index gathers contents about the same subject, such as mathematics. The left-side menu gives access to all the indexes of History Tracers.

To open an index, expand a section in the menu and click its option. For example, under Games, click Math. You can also reach an index through a link.

The index page lists its contents organized by headings. Each entry has a name and a short description. Click a name to open that content.

When you open a content from an index, a navigation table appears at the top and at the bottom of the page. It has three columns. Previous opens the content before. The middle column returns to the index. Next opens the content after.

Because the table is repeated at the bottom, you can move to the next content without scrolling back to the top.

Open the Mathematical Games index and try the navigation for yourself.
